-- The atom sync handshake does not start itself -- see `sync.luau` for why it
-- is a module. This is the one line that starts it, for a template that has no
-- server boot list of its own yet.
--
-- A GAME WITH A BOOT LIST SHOULD DELETE THIS FILE and call
-- `require(ServerScriptService.Server.net.sync).start()` from that list instead,
-- first, before anything that registers an atom. `start()` is idempotent, so
-- doing both is harmless rather than wrong -- but then the ORDER is back to
-- whatever order the engine ran the scripts in, which is the thing the module
-- shape exists to take back.
require(script.Parent.sync).start()
